through the EMA readiness index only. Regression test `test_mineral_suppression_is_applied_once_in_spawning` passes.","Light-depth probe now shows net positive shallow growth: 0.6301g (shallow) vs 0.2785g (deep), both positive, with an explicit `growth_shallow > 0.0` assertion (`light_depth_positive_growth`). Doc comment correctly describes the mechanism.","Equipment-scaling tolerance tightened from 0.55 to 0.40 at line 1226; probe passes with current divergence (~32% TAN, ~39% DO range) within the 40% envelope.","Clippy passes clean on the habitat test file: `cargo clippy -p tank_harness --test e2e_habitat_geometry_probes` — no warnings.","All 5 acceptance criteria scenarios present as named test functions with doc comments: biofilter_scaling, light_depth, habitat_fouling, substrate_redox, equipment_scaling.","Summary test `all_habitat_geometry_probes_summary` runs all 5 probes, prints structured pass/fail report, and returns Err on any failure (non-zero exit).","Assertions use directional comparisons (A > B) and envelope ranges (min/max tolerance bands), not exact values — resilient to reasonable retuning.","Equipment scaling uses a paired 1× vs 2× geometry run with proportionally scaled hardware, plants (both guilds), and stocking (volume-cubed scaling); per-liter concentrations compared within 40% tolerance via `record_within_fraction()`."],"findings_or_gaps":["Uncommitted working-directory changes from parallel projects (tanksim-6e5.6.4 and others) break the biofilter scaling probe on the working tree — the committed checkpoint is clean, but any merge/rebase integrating those changes will need to re-validate biofilter assertions.","The `tank_scenarios` crate has uncommitted additions referencing 16 `ShrimpPreset` fields (density_repro_half_suppression_per_l, tan_repro_threshold_mg_n_per_l, etc.) that don't exist on the struct yet — this is from a parallel project and doesn't affect the committed checkpoint, but will cause a compile error when those changes land.","Hatch rate (shrimp.rs:890) still uses `f_mineral` directly, which is correct because hatch doesn't use the EMA readiness, but the asymmetry with spawning could be confusing without an inline comment explaining why."],"follow_up_or_amendments":["When merging parallel worktree changes (especially the shrimp instability tracker sum→max change and the biofilter probe refactor), re-run the full habitat/geometry probe suite to catch the biofilter_reduced_n_exposure regression observed in the working tree.","Consider adding a brief inline comment near hatch_rate's f_mineral usage clarifying that hatch intentionally applies mineral suppression outside the EMA path, to prevent future confusion about the spawn_rate fix."]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"a244d37c-6f3a-44d9-ab80-0a25cc830582"}
